 area in the specimen were chosen as Fe, Mo, and Ti standards. The measured X-ray intensity for each element was corrected and then converted into its concentration by a computer program. The Camebax-Micro set was often calibrated by measuring the pure metals to ascertain that the working condition for the EPMA remains stable during the measurement.","quote_chars_original":505,"quote_clipped":true,"second_reader_agrees":true,"type":"measurement"},{"extraction_accepted":false,"has_dropped_fields":true,"id":"ORC-WZ3GWSIY3O","label":"diffusion couples of the ternary Fe-Mo-Ti system","nominal_composition":"Fe-Mo-Ti","page":1,"quote":"Metal Ti was cut into 6 • 12 x 15 mm, whereas Fe and Mo were cut into 6 x 6 x 15 mm. In a similar technique used in a previous w o r k , 161 the diffusion couples of the ternary Fe-Mo-Ti system were prepared by tying the three different metal pieces together using pure Mo wire, as illustrated in Figure 3. In order to obtain good contact among different metals in the diffusion couples, each metal piece was ground flat before tying.","quote_chars_original":591,"quote_clipped":true,"second_reader_agrees":false,"starting_materials":"pure iron (Fe > 99.9 wt pct), pure molybdenum (Mo > 99.5 wt pct), and pure titanium (Ti > 99.5 wt pct)","synthesis":"In a similar technique used in a previous w o r k , 161 the diffusion couples of the ternary Fe-Mo-Ti system were prepared by tying the three different metal pieces together using pure Mo wire, as illustrated in Figure 3. In order to obtain good contact among different metals in the diffusion couples, each metal piece was ground flat before tying.","type":"sample"},{"atmosphere_or_container":"sealed in a silica capsule under vacuum (0.0133 Pa)","cooling":"air-cooled by breaking the capsule","duration":"480 hours","duration_parsed":{"hours":480.0,"printed":"480 hours"},"extraction_accepted":true,"has_dropped_fields":true,"id":"ORC-GRB6O72DRL","page":1,"purpose":"heat treated","quote":"These specimens s